# Layout Rendering

Canon applies: the CSS box model, Flexbox and Grid sizing (intrinsic and extrinsic sizing),
CSS Logical Properties, and WCAG 2.2 1.4.10 Reflow with its two-dimensional-content exception.
This rule holds only this project's decisions for rendered geometry. Taste and the UI tell
catalog are `ui-anti-slop.mdc`.

## Rules

1. **A layout claim is measured in a real layout engine.** The project's real-CSS tier
   (Storybook, Playwright, a component-visual suite) or a probe that mounts the component and
   reads computed CSS off the node. A DOM stub (happy-dom, jsdom) loads no stylesheet, so a
   class assertion or a `getBoundingClientRect` there measures nothing. Measurements supplied
   with the change count when they name the command and the viewport.
2. **320px is always a supported width.** Other supported widths come from the project's own
   list: `DESIGN.md`, the brief, the job context, or the hosts the product ships in. At every
   supported width nothing is clipped and the page does not scroll sideways.
3. **Identical data renders identical geometry in every locale.** A box sized by its own
   labels is measured with the longest real translation in the catalog, not the English one.
4. **A component that mirrors under RTL mirrors entirely.** Logical properties flip; a physical
   gradient, shadow or transform in the same component is made logical or flipped explicitly.
   Surfaces that do not mirror by platform practice (media controls and their seek bar, numbers,
   code, phone numbers) keep `dir="ltr"` with the reason in a comment.

---

## Review severities (shared with reviewers)

`review-layout` rates these by this table, and `review-ui-ux` defers overflow and reflow to it.
Change a row here, never in a reviewer. A row counts only when the change touches the element.

| Signal | A finding when | Default | Not a finding |
|---|---|---|---|
| Element renders at 0px while its label shows (Rule 1) | at a supported width, measured | `major` | a width no supported host reaches (`info`) |
| Identical data renders different geometry per locale (Rule 3) | measured with the longest real translation in the catalog | `major` | — |
| Content clipped, or the page scrolls sideways (Rule 2) | at a supported width, 320px included, measured | `major` | content that needs two dimensions to read (data table, map, code block) scrolling inside its own region |
| Cosmetic offset (a few px off centre), or a physical gradient, shadow or transform that does not flip under RTL (Rule 4) | measured: a few px, or one direction named per locale | `minor` | a surface that does not mirror by platform practice, with its reason read |
| Any layout claim with no measurement (Rule 1) | always | `info` | — |
